{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch1oQt5sbGcwBFFeCsGQA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"mode\":\"self\",\"summary\":\"Captain Semicolon builds this alone. It's all backend groundwork: the Node project, the tiny server, the split math module with its test, and a placeholder page. Pete and Twinkle take over the real page and the styles in the next items.\",\"subtasks\":[{\"text\":\"Set up the Node project, server, split math and its test\",\"assignee\":\"a-semic\",\"brief\":\"Make a plain Node project with no dependencies: a package.json with \\\"start\\\": \\\"node server.js\\\" and \\\"test\\\": \\\"node --test\\\". Write server.js using only Node's built-in http module to serve static files from public/, with a simple placeholder public/index.html. Add src/split.js. It takes bill amount, tip % and number of people and returns the tip, the total and what each person pays, rounded to cents. Bad input (empty fields, letters, negative numbers, zero or fractional people) must give a clear, safe result and never crash. Add src/split.test.js using node:test, covering normal cases, rounding to cents and bad input. Put `run: node server.js` as one line in .project. In CLAUDE.md under \\\"Project-specific rules\\\", write the stack (plain Node, no dependencies), how to run it (`node server.js`) and how to test it (`node --test`). Done when the server starts, the placeholder page loads in a browser and `node --test` passes.\",\"parallel\":true}]}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3647,"cache_read_input_tokens":4575,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3647},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0eed3